WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.250
Anna, here's your coffee.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:04.430
Thanks, Marsha.

3
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:05.950
What's wrong?

4
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.550
I'm thinking about my family.

5
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.970
I'm feeling homesick.

6
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.430
Do you want to talk about it?

7
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.830
Sure! I have some photos.

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.870
Yes. Yes, you do!

9
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.130
Photos really help.

10
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.570
This is my mother and this is my father.

11
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.430
They are rodeo clowns.

12
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.470
What do rodeo clowns do?

13
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.450
They make jokes at a rodeo.

14
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.290
They make people laugh.

15
00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.830
That-That's very different.

16
00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:20.650
Who is that woman in the picture?

17
00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.510
That is my Aunt Lavender.

18
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.870
She is my mom's sister.

19
00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.770
She loves gardening and makes spoons.

20
00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.490
She makes spoons?

21
00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:34.810
Of course.

22
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.310
That, too, is very different.

23
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.970
Oh! This is my Uncle John.

24
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.970
He is my father's brother.

25
00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.810
What does Uncle John do?

26
00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.230
He's a chicken farmer.

27
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.610
And makes guitars.

28
00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:54.490
He's awesome, and I'm his favorite niece.

29
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.050
Who are they?

30
00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.850
They are my cousins.

31
00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.630
They are my Uncle John's daughter and son.
